WEBVTT

00:12.270 --> 00:13.890
Here you are.

00:13.890 --> 00:17.220
This drink warms you up 
and helps with fatigue.

00:17.220 --> 00:18.320
Thank you.

00:32.210 --> 00:38.920
<b>Banished from the Hero's Party,
I Decided to Live a Quiet Life in the Countryside 2nd</b>

01:49.490 --> 01:53.500
<b>The Gem Beast</b>

01:49.490 --> 01:53.500
<b>The Gem Beast</b>

01:54.000 --> 01:57.130
You used to drop by often to drink 
this when we were in Central.

01:59.290 --> 02:00.450
It's delicious.

02:01.700 --> 02:06.350
Gideon, I'm glad we could 
have such a peaceful reunion.

02:06.690 --> 02:08.810
Sorry I made you worry.

02:09.060 --> 02:14.450
Don't be. What's more, I was happy to hear 
that you two are living together now!

02:17.490 --> 02:19.660
On that note, I have a suggestion.

02:20.500 --> 02:24.080
Would you like to move to the 
Kingdom of Kiramin with me?

02:24.080 --> 02:24.790
What?

02:24.790 --> 02:25.790
Nope.

02:28.050 --> 02:29.250
Well, hear me out first.

02:30.200 --> 02:34.710
Kiramin is the biggest city-state 
on the continent of Avalon.

02:35.420 --> 02:41.170
It lies in the cold northern plains, 
but magic keeps the weather springlike.

02:41.890 --> 02:45.620
Most of all, while high elves 
are by no means perfect,

02:45.620 --> 02:48.560
we never betray our friends and allies.

02:49.520 --> 02:51.520
Well, that came out of nowhere.

02:51.740 --> 02:53.180
Not true!

02:54.270 --> 02:56.650
I never could make sense of it.

02:57.220 --> 03:01.610
Why were you kicked out of the party when 
you always worked so hard for everyone?

03:02.220 --> 03:07.870
It was inevitable. 
I could no longer keep up in battle.

03:08.080 --> 03:11.690
"Inevitable"?! Not you, too!

03:12.460 --> 03:15.730
Even if you really had 
turned into dead weight,

03:15.730 --> 03:18.510
I wanted to adventure with you.

03:19.000 --> 03:22.530
If you were having a tough time, 
I wanted to be your pillar of support.

03:23.560 --> 03:28.500
Dumping a guy who's always been there for 
you just because he "stopped being useful"

03:29.190 --> 03:30.730
is not an option in my mind!

03:31.010 --> 03:33.520
I appreciate the sentiment, Yarandrala.

03:34.100 --> 03:35.060
But...

03:35.060 --> 03:36.430
You too, Rit!

03:36.430 --> 03:38.430
You're a Loggervian princess

03:38.430 --> 03:41.360
and a hero who has fought 
countless battles for your homeland!

03:41.360 --> 03:45.310
Yet you wound up having to leave 
your home all by yourself, too.

03:45.310 --> 03:49.600
I-I did, but that was my idea.

03:49.600 --> 03:51.990
Nobody was in the wrong.

03:51.990 --> 03:55.920
Well, I wouldn't have let 
you set off alone like that.

03:57.480 --> 03:58.650
Yarandrala.

03:59.460 --> 04:02.060
We're thankful for how 
much you care about us,

04:02.060 --> 04:05.140
but we aren't going to go to Kiramin.

04:05.140 --> 04:06.460
Why?!

04:06.460 --> 04:11.580
Because we're living happy 
lives here in Zoltan.

04:12.410 --> 04:13.160
Yeah.

04:13.780 --> 04:17.830
At first, I only came here because 
I thought nobody would recognize me,

04:17.830 --> 04:20.750
but now, I've developed great 
friendships with the people of Zoltan.

04:20.750 --> 04:23.320
What if you get betrayed again, though?

04:23.930 --> 04:25.280
Then that's fine.

04:27.730 --> 04:29.370
When someone invites me out for drinks,

04:30.250 --> 04:33.360
and I say I won't go without Rit,

04:33.360 --> 04:38.300
they'll tease me about it, but then immediately 
start planning a family dinner party.

04:39.400 --> 04:42.170
That kind of relationship 
is more than enough for me.

04:47.410 --> 04:48.450
I know.

04:48.450 --> 04:51.750
Why don't you live in 
Zoltan for a while, too?

04:52.320 --> 04:55.510
Yeah. It's a really nice place.

04:55.510 --> 04:57.780
Maybe, but Kiramin's much better—

04:59.240 --> 05:01.340
It's starting to get a little chilly.

05:01.340 --> 05:03.030
Let's have another cup of tea.

05:03.030 --> 05:04.900
In that case...

05:05.350 --> 05:06.180
Tisse?!

05:06.180 --> 05:09.180
I know just the place to warm up.

05:12.830 --> 05:15.330
This bath is perfect.

05:15.330 --> 05:17.670
It soothes both the mind and body.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.290
Yup. This feels good.

05:20.880 --> 05:21.810
And also...

05:26.530 --> 05:27.550
Such a pretty view.

05:31.160 --> 05:33.600
I'm happy for you, Ruti.

05:35.890 --> 05:36.850
Thanks.

05:37.320 --> 05:40.630
The water's hot, and the view's unbelievable.

05:40.630 --> 05:44.820
This merits a high score. 
I'm going to say 95.

05:44.820 --> 05:46.860
Where'd it lose the five points?

05:46.860 --> 05:49.680
It's much too far from Zoltan.

05:49.680 --> 05:50.820
Ah.

05:52.020 --> 05:53.370
I guess.

05:54.110 --> 05:56.970
We'll be arriving at the 
gem giants' settlement soon.

05:57.520 --> 05:59.380
I wonder what kind of monsters they are.

05:59.860 --> 06:03.460
I hear they gain energy from cutting gems.

06:03.710 --> 06:04.880
They do?

06:04.880 --> 06:09.000
I assume it's like what eating is for us.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.670
Something essential for survival.

06:11.670 --> 06:13.470
Like eating, huh?

06:13.470 --> 06:14.220
Hup!

06:16.100 --> 06:17.390
Yum!

06:17.390 --> 06:19.480
Okay, that's not too relatable.

06:20.180 --> 06:23.500
So, the gem giants have the 
stone you're looking for?

06:23.500 --> 06:30.230
Yeah. We're going to trade the 
Zoltatian glass Red has for a blue sapphire.

06:30.230 --> 06:34.000
The artistry in Zoltatian 
glass is unique to Zoltan,

06:34.000 --> 06:37.260
so Red was sure they would like it.

06:37.260 --> 06:38.250
Huh...

06:38.650 --> 06:40.370
Good for you, Rit.

06:41.840 --> 06:43.740
Where are Red and the others, by the way?

06:44.980 --> 06:47.380
Mogrim hates baths to begin with,

06:47.630 --> 06:51.190
and Red's being considerate 
and using the annex bath.

06:51.190 --> 06:54.350
What? He's taking a dip all alone?

06:54.350 --> 06:56.080
I feel bad for him!

06:56.080 --> 06:58.890
Hey, wait, Yarandrala.

06:58.890 --> 07:00.100
Hold up!

07:00.500 --> 07:01.920
Don't be a stranger, Gideon!

07:01.920 --> 07:04.000
You can't do this, Yarandrala!

07:04.660 --> 07:08.130
Hurry up and get in with us already!

07:09.990 --> 07:13.490
By the way, milady, are you okay with this?

07:13.490 --> 07:14.520
With what?

07:14.520 --> 07:17.430
Red and Rit getting married.

07:17.920 --> 07:18.590
Oh...

07:19.520 --> 07:24.050
Rit's a nice girl, and she'll 
treat my big brother well.

07:24.750 --> 07:29.010
I always thought she was the kind 
of person I wanted him to marry.

07:29.400 --> 07:30.760
Is that so?

07:31.410 --> 07:35.510
Does the thought of their 
marriage not make you lonely?

07:36.000 --> 07:38.020
Well, I'm his sister.

07:38.020 --> 07:40.460
I can't marry him.

07:40.950 --> 07:45.520
So I'll let Rit take the role of his wife.

07:45.850 --> 07:47.340
Milady...

07:48.170 --> 07:52.990
But I can still be his lover.

07:54.930 --> 07:58.620
Big Brother is a giving person. 
He can handle two partners with ease.

07:59.280 --> 08:04.370
Rit can be the number one wife, 
and I can be his number one lover.

08:05.570 --> 08:07.800
I'm going to join him, too.

08:18.200 --> 08:19.400
What?!

08:19.400 --> 08:22.680
You asked Red and them to move to Kiramin?!

08:22.930 --> 08:27.150
I did. They can live happier lives there.

08:28.480 --> 08:31.780
Don't make 'em mingle with 
you lawless high elves!

08:31.780 --> 08:35.460
They're much better off living 
in Zoltan with us dwarves!

08:35.460 --> 08:36.370
Hmph!

08:36.370 --> 08:40.320
High elves and dwarves really 
don't get along, huh?

08:46.490 --> 08:48.960
Are those the gem giants?

08:49.450 --> 08:51.150
Something seems off with them.

08:55.130 --> 08:59.640
I'm ashamed to say we have nothing 
to offer to make you feel welcome,

09:00.000 --> 09:02.010
but please, make yourselves at home.

09:02.010 --> 09:03.080
Thank you.

09:03.080 --> 09:05.880
We're here to trade for your gems.

09:05.880 --> 09:08.540
And we can offer this Zoltatian glass.

09:13.230 --> 09:14.550
It's beautiful.

09:14.970 --> 09:18.940
Truly valuable for us 
as a species. However...

09:19.590 --> 09:22.040
Unfortunately, we cannot make that trade,

09:22.480 --> 09:25.210
for we do not have any 
gems to offer in exchange.

09:34.870 --> 09:35.760
Stop that!

09:41.670 --> 09:42.800
You can have this.

09:42.800 --> 09:43.730
Really?

09:46.350 --> 09:47.890
Thanks!

09:49.860 --> 09:52.400
Look what I got, Mom!

10:01.270 --> 10:02.970
Wow...

10:02.970 --> 10:04.450
We have more glass.

10:04.890 --> 10:07.770
It isn't much, but please 
share it amongst yourselves.

10:10.080 --> 10:11.400
But...

10:11.400 --> 10:12.680
Don't worry about compensating us.

10:13.690 --> 10:17.450
I'm not sure why, but you 
don't have any gems, right?

10:17.940 --> 10:20.390
If this keeps up, you'll all starve to death.

10:21.040 --> 10:22.700
So please accept it.

10:28.770 --> 10:31.030
Do <i>not</i> drop them.

10:31.030 --> 10:33.020
Don't worry. I've got this.

10:33.020 --> 10:35.130
This will put smiles on all their faces.

10:36.030 --> 10:37.030
Very well.

10:37.570 --> 10:41.990
We are truly grateful for receiving 
such a blessing in these trying times.

10:42.980 --> 10:46.370
Our human, dwarven, and high elven friends...

10:46.370 --> 10:51.270
We promise to you an unchanging friendship 
until the day our tribe dies out.

10:58.350 --> 11:02.950
Why do you think Demis 
created them like that?

11:02.950 --> 11:06.460
You mean how they gain 
energy from cutting gems?

11:06.460 --> 11:07.020
Yep.

11:07.680 --> 11:10.070
The Almighty created this world.

11:10.070 --> 11:13.110
Every living being was surely 
crafted with a purpose.

11:13.500 --> 11:19.650
By defeating gem giants, humans can 
obtain gems as their victory spoils.

11:20.310 --> 11:25.870
And maybe they were meant to be enemies
 to fight in order to develop our Blessings.

11:26.450 --> 11:30.160
If the Almighty really designed things 
that way, then battle is unavoidable.

11:30.650 --> 11:31.420
But...

11:31.780 --> 11:35.170
Monsters exist to be more than 
just fodder for Blessings.

11:35.740 --> 11:37.310
That's what I would like to believe.

11:37.310 --> 11:39.680
Yeah, I feel the same way.

11:43.050 --> 11:45.990
It's been a while since we've 
been able to cut our fill.

11:45.990 --> 11:47.560
You have our heartfelt gratitude.

11:47.840 --> 11:50.810
So, what's happening in your settlement?

11:52.560 --> 11:55.310
A troublesome beast has started living here.

11:55.530 --> 11:56.700
What beast?

11:56.700 --> 12:00.350
A gem beast—a monster that eats gems.

12:00.350 --> 12:01.740
A gem beast?

12:01.740 --> 12:07.220
Just by existing, it turns all the gems 
and minerals in its vicinity into lead.

12:07.220 --> 12:08.380
Lead?

12:08.380 --> 12:09.040
Indeed.

12:09.760 --> 12:11.940
And this is that lead.

12:11.940 --> 12:14.970
It seems subtly imbued with magic.

12:14.970 --> 12:18.000
It's also more poisonous now.

12:18.560 --> 12:23.990
If this has contaminated the groundwater, 
this entire region is in danger.

12:23.990 --> 12:27.130
That may be why the zoogs' 
forest has been weakened.

12:27.130 --> 12:29.810
We need to stop this before 
the damage spreads.

12:29.810 --> 12:33.460
But we've never heard of this monster before.

12:33.460 --> 12:35.170
How will we fight it?

12:35.170 --> 12:37.570
I remember reading something in 
historical records before.

12:38.020 --> 12:44.320
It said that a warrior party set out to 
fight a gem beast in the era of wood elves.

12:44.320 --> 12:46.940
How did those warriors defeat it?

12:46.940 --> 12:48.900
Nah, they didn't.

12:48.900 --> 12:49.990
What?!

12:50.290 --> 12:52.930
Most of the wood elves in the battle died,

12:52.930 --> 12:56.570
and only a handful of 
warriors managed to escape.

12:56.570 --> 13:00.250
So, no one has ever defeated that thing?

13:00.560 --> 13:03.150
Our fighters fell to it, too.

13:03.150 --> 13:05.130
There is no guarantee 
you would return alive.

13:06.130 --> 13:06.640
Still...

13:07.260 --> 13:09.140
We can't let it be.

13:12.610 --> 13:17.230
This must be the southern mine 
the tribal chief mentioned.

13:17.530 --> 13:20.530
There are still gems remaining here.

13:20.530 --> 13:22.870
The beast may show up to consume them.

13:22.870 --> 13:25.130
The thing's apparently huge...

13:25.130 --> 13:28.660
But there are plenty of hiding spots here,

13:28.660 --> 13:31.090
and we brought a whole bunch of potions, too.

13:32.560 --> 13:34.080
Never seen this rock before.

13:34.080 --> 13:36.500
Mogrim, try to stick close!

13:36.500 --> 13:38.380
Right! My bad!

13:44.470 --> 13:45.220
Big Brother!

13:57.110 --> 13:58.940
The rock wall turned to lead?!

14:27.230 --> 14:30.150
So that's the gem beast.

14:40.940 --> 14:41.860
Ruti?!

14:43.560 --> 14:45.070
Sacred Shield.

14:52.460 --> 14:53.530
It's shattering.

14:57.470 --> 14:58.780
Ruti!

15:07.700 --> 15:09.300
Thorn Bind!

15:33.360 --> 15:35.030
It must have a vulnerability somewhere.

15:56.300 --> 15:58.720
The impact was weaker than I expected.

15:59.020 --> 16:02.300
Given how big it is, it could've 
made the entire mountain crumble.

16:03.140 --> 16:05.690
Is it propping up its whole body with magic?

16:08.390 --> 16:10.070
My Sacred Shield?

16:17.470 --> 16:18.620
My Thorn Bind?

16:26.380 --> 16:27.380
Are you kidding me?!

16:28.090 --> 16:29.530
Sacred Shield.

16:34.790 --> 16:39.020
It can replicate its opponents' magic spells?

16:39.020 --> 16:41.180
What a troublesome foe.

16:47.360 --> 16:50.800
It can use fire and water magic 
at the same time? That's absurd!

16:50.800 --> 16:52.620
What's going on with its Blessing?!

16:55.700 --> 16:57.490
Wait, could the gem beast be...

16:57.940 --> 17:00.870
...using multiple Blessings to 
boost its physical abilities.

17:01.120 --> 17:06.040
That's why it can reflect physical and 
magical attacks, and support its massive weight.

17:06.460 --> 17:07.660
In which case...

17:08.330 --> 17:09.500
You don't mean...

17:31.000 --> 17:32.580
Sacred Shield.

17:40.580 --> 17:41.580
Did that work?!

17:45.660 --> 17:47.370
What now, Red?

17:47.370 --> 17:51.190
Lowering its Blessing level might help.

17:51.190 --> 17:52.450
For that...

17:52.450 --> 17:54.260
We need the wild elves' medicine, yes?

17:54.470 --> 17:57.260
Yeah. I think this is our best bet.

17:57.520 --> 17:59.510
Is that the thing you used against Ademi?

17:59.510 --> 18:03.520
That's right. But making it 
drink this won't be easy.

18:03.760 --> 18:05.020
I'll stop it.

18:05.240 --> 18:05.900
Use this.

18:05.900 --> 18:06.940
Thanks.

18:11.980 --> 18:15.360
O origin of mana, ruler of all creation...

18:15.800 --> 18:17.670
Great spirit of the mighty tree!

18:41.210 --> 18:41.890
Take that!

19:04.330 --> 19:08.540
This thing can't even stand 
without its Blessings?

19:32.240 --> 19:33.280
Man...

19:33.280 --> 19:37.540
I didn't expect to find this beauty 
inside the gem beast's body.

19:37.540 --> 19:41.280
I'm glad you got the earth 
crystal you came for.

19:41.280 --> 19:45.340
Aye! With this, the childbirth 
should go smoothly.

19:46.730 --> 19:48.380
On the other hand...

19:51.260 --> 19:52.210
Wow.

19:52.210 --> 19:53.720
Such a pretty view.

19:53.720 --> 19:54.450
Yeah.

19:54.890 --> 19:56.480
I'll be home soon.

19:56.480 --> 19:58.650
Wait for me!

20:03.150 --> 20:06.970
Red, Rit, you two are content 
with your current lives, yes?

20:07.240 --> 20:07.940
Yeah.

20:08.380 --> 20:12.980
I plan to continue leading a perfectly 
normal life together with Rit.

20:13.450 --> 20:15.980
And you can do that in Zoltan?

20:16.430 --> 20:17.040
Yeah.

20:17.600 --> 20:21.190
For the first time in my life, 
I'm living for myself.

20:22.670 --> 20:23.740
Good to know.

20:24.520 --> 20:28.680
I've decided to try living 
in Zoltan for a while.

20:28.680 --> 20:30.310
What? Really?

20:30.310 --> 20:34.170
I've taken an interest in the place 
that gives you two so much joy.

20:34.170 --> 20:36.500
Yeah? We'd love to have you!

20:36.880 --> 20:38.750
Is that okay, Ruti?

20:39.410 --> 20:40.130
Of course.

20:40.790 --> 20:43.990
Better get everyone together 
for a welcoming party.

20:43.990 --> 20:47.710
Hurry up! Or I'll leave you behind!

20:49.760 --> 20:50.470
Ljubo.

20:51.010 --> 20:53.330
I believe I am plenty strong now.

20:53.840 --> 20:58.110
I would like to join the front lines as 
the hero and fight the demon lord's army.

20:59.030 --> 21:02.320
Van, you mustn't rush things.

21:02.320 --> 21:05.910
We should plan everything out 
and execute it flawlessly.

21:05.910 --> 21:09.440
I have prepared a new battlefield for you.

21:09.440 --> 21:12.980
Head out with Esta to defeat this monster...

21:13.600 --> 21:14.380
Come in.

21:16.900 --> 21:17.840
It's fine.

21:19.480 --> 21:23.050
There has been a sighting of the
 former demon lord's airship.

21:23.370 --> 21:25.830
The demon lord's vessel?!

21:25.830 --> 21:28.830
It was supposedly headed for 
the remote town of Zoltan.

21:31.490 --> 21:32.610
Zoltan...

21:33.680 --> 21:37.470
Kiggith should be back 
from his scouting mission.

21:37.470 --> 21:40.300
Have him head to Zoltan.

21:40.300 --> 21:40.900
Sire.

21:42.440 --> 21:43.350
Ljubo—

21:43.940 --> 21:49.200
Building strength suitable for a hero and 
leveling up your Blessing comes first.

21:49.430 --> 21:50.920
Precisely.

21:50.920 --> 21:55.580
Stick to the plan and go monster 
hunting with Esta for the time being.

21:55.940 --> 21:59.000
I'll make sure Zoltan is 
thoroughly investigated.

21:59.580 --> 22:02.270
Oh, don't you worry.

22:02.270 --> 22:05.470
I'll draft up a brand-new plan for you, too.

22:06.140 --> 22:06.850
Thank you.
